# =============================================================================
# Build output
# =============================================================================
# 32 GB at the time of writing, and entirely reproducible.
/target/
**/target/

# =============================================================================
# Third-party test suites — fetched, deliberately not vendored
# =============================================================================
# `scripts/fetch-testsuites.sh` clones the W3C RDF and SPARQL suites here. They are
# ~64 MB of third-party fixtures under a different licence, and each carries its own
# nested `.git` — committing them would either bloat the tree or leave a dangling
# submodule reference. Without them the conformance tests skip rather than fail, so a
# fresh checkout still builds and tests green.
/testsuites/

# =============================================================================
# Local configuration and secrets
# =============================================================================
# `deploy/holos.env` is committed as the documented template; the `.local` override is
# where a deployment puts its own values and must never be.
deploy/holos.env.local
*.env.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# TLS material. `deploy/nginx.conf` references certificate and key paths, and a private
# key reaching a remote is unrecoverable — rotation is the only remedy.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore

# Credentials that tend to appear beside a deployment.
*credentials*
*secret*
!**/*secrets*.md
.htpasswd
.netrc

# =============================================================================
# Store data and runtime state
# =============================================================================
# The default store directory in `deploy/holos.env`, plus the backup destination.
/var/
**/var/store/
**/var/backups/

# RocksDB leaves these wherever a store was opened. Listing them by name catches a store
# created outside the conventional directory — including by a test run that was
# interrupted before it could clean up.
LOCK
CURRENT
IDENTITY
MANIFEST-*
OPTIONS-*
*.sst
*.ldb
LOG
LOG.old.*

# =============================================================================
# Benchmark working files
# =============================================================================
# `holos-bench` generates these; they are large and reproducible from the harness. By
# default it writes them to the system temp directory rather than the tree, so these
# patterns only matter when HOLOS_BENCH_DIR points somewhere inside it.
#
# There was a `holos-bench/` rule here. Without a leading slash that matches at any depth,
# so it excluded `crates/holos-bench/` — the crate's own source — from the repository. A
# fresh clone then had a workspace member with no manifest, and `cargo build` failed before
# compiling anything. Do not reinstate it: the data never lands in the tree anyway.
bench-*.nt
bench-*.nq
/bench/

# =============================================================================
# Python
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.Python

# =============================================================================
# Editors and operating systems
# =============================================================================
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# =============================================================================
# Deliberately NOT ignored — listed so nobody adds them by reflex
# =============================================================================
# Cargo.lock         — this workspace ships binaries (`holos`, `holos-server`), so the
#                      lock file is part of what makes a build reproducible.
# conformance/*.failures
#                    — the ratchet baselines. Ignoring them would silence the thing that
#                      catches a conformance regression.
# deploy/holos.env   — the documented template, with no values in it.
# docs/*.html        — the published design study and manual.
